1
00:02:25,189 --> 00:02:26,065
You know him?

2
00:02:26,065 --> 00:02:27,650
He's Caileigh's dad.

3
00:02:28,612 --> 00:02:29,738
I—Impossible.

4
00:02:29,902 --> 00:02:31,403
You cannot trust anyone.

5
00:02:31,403 --> 00:02:32,446
What's the plan, boss?

6
00:02:32,446 --> 00:02:33,948
She has a daughter, huh?

7
00:02:36,325 --> 00:02:36,909
Kill her.

8
00:02:36,909 --> 00:02:39,119
You're not laying a
finger on my friend.

9
00:02:39,244 --> 00:02:40,554
And that's final.

10
00:02:40,579 --> 00:02:42,281
Were you the one
who did that to Young?

11
00:02:46,669 --> 00:02:48,712
Age does really matter.

12
00:02:49,254 --> 00:02:50,839
You're too young to surpass me.

13
00:02:52,967 --> 00:02:54,802
You're trapped with me now.

14
00:02:54,927 --> 00:02:55,719
Shout,

15
00:02:56,136 --> 00:02:57,513
and I'll cut your throat.

16
00:02:58,764 --> 00:02:59,556
Hi, miss.

17
00:02:59,556 --> 00:03:01,141
Looks like you're
all alone here.

18
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:02,851
Seems like your
ride's taking a while.

19
00:03:02,851 --> 00:03:04,144
Ezekiel Roswell.

20
00:03:04,269 --> 00:03:05,145
Everyone!

21
00:03:06,021 --> 00:03:07,064
Look for my wife!

22
00:03:07,898 --> 00:03:08,540
Now!

23
00:03:08,565 --> 00:03:09,694
Now! Move it!

24
00:03:10,526 --> 00:03:11,460
Whoa!

25
00:03:12,027 --> 00:03:13,237
That's so unfair!

26
00:03:13,237 --> 00:03:14,989
I keep losing. I don't
wanna play anymore.

27
00:03:14,989 --> 00:03:17,199
Sorry, rules are rules.

28
00:03:17,324 --> 00:03:19,451
So, for your last question,

29
00:03:19,618 --> 00:03:24,456
What was Roswell's
last order to his men?

30
00:03:25,541 --> 00:03:26,517
Fuck shit!

31
00:03:26,542 --> 00:03:27,410
Fuck!

32
00:03:27,751 --> 00:03:30,129
I really don't know how
that blueprint disappeared.

33
00:03:30,504 --> 00:03:31,449
Damn it!

34
00:03:31,964 --> 00:03:32,817
Fuck!

35
00:03:40,014 --> 00:03:41,140
Who's that?

36
00:03:43,434 --> 00:03:45,894
What the fuck are
you doing here?

37
00:03:46,228 --> 00:03:48,397
Venice, someone
might've followed you.

38
00:03:48,397 --> 00:03:49,440
Don't worry.

39
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:50,858
No one followed me.

40
00:03:50,858 --> 00:03:51,859
Okay?

41
00:03:52,401 --> 00:03:54,361
So, what happened?

42
00:03:54,778 --> 00:03:56,739
Fuck, the blueprint's gone.

43
00:03:57,573 --> 00:03:58,615
Relax.

44
00:03:58,741 --> 00:04:01,035
I can just ask
Aemie for another one.

45
00:04:01,326 --> 00:04:02,261
Huh?

46
00:04:02,286 --> 00:04:03,162
Are you stupid?

47
00:04:04,413 --> 00:04:05,998
What if Roswell finds out?

48
00:04:06,248 --> 00:04:06,749
Huh?

49
00:04:08,333 --> 00:04:09,626
Alright, cuz.

50
00:04:10,544 --> 00:04:11,685
Don't worry.

51
00:04:11,754 --> 00:04:12,755
I'll have it.

52
00:04:14,715 --> 00:04:17,176
Whatever it takes.

53
00:05:38,382 --> 00:05:40,717
Dong! I have—

54
00:05:44,054 --> 00:05:44,958
You're safe.

55
00:05:46,181 --> 00:05:47,036
Whoa.

56
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:50,727
Missed me already?

57
00:05:51,478 --> 00:05:52,938
I'm okay, Dong.

58
00:05:59,278 --> 00:06:00,133
Whoa.

59
00:06:02,698 --> 00:06:04,366
Oh my god.

60
00:06:06,034 --> 00:06:07,995
Were we robbed?

61
00:06:08,871 --> 00:06:10,080
Where the hell have you been?

62
00:06:11,665 --> 00:06:12,457
Just went out to eat.

63
00:06:12,457 --> 00:06:13,458
Eat?

64
00:06:13,831 --> 00:06:15,792
You didn't even tell me
you were going out to eat?

65
00:06:16,837 --> 00:06:18,547
I was with your friends.

66
00:06:19,381 --> 00:06:20,234
Friends?

67
00:06:21,216 --> 00:06:22,551
The last time I checked,

68
00:06:22,551 --> 00:06:25,345
I don't have friends and
never will be having one.

69
00:06:27,347 --> 00:06:28,515
Whoa.

70
00:06:28,682 --> 00:06:30,392
He says he doesn't have friends.

71
00:06:30,726 --> 00:06:31,643
Then what are you?

72
00:06:34,354 --> 00:06:35,689
Why are you mad, Dong?

73
00:06:35,689 --> 00:06:37,232
Because I was worried.

74
00:06:39,443 --> 00:06:42,029
Is going off with
strangers your new hobby?

75
00:06:42,279 --> 00:06:42,988
Hey, no!

76
00:06:42,988 --> 00:06:44,406
They introduced themselves to me.

77
00:06:47,117 --> 00:06:48,118
Let's talk.

78
00:06:52,539 --> 00:06:53,540
Look at this guy.

79
00:06:53,624 --> 00:06:56,752
He says he wants to talk.
But then he goes and leaves me.

80
00:06:59,254 --> 00:07:00,255
Zeke.

81
00:07:07,804 --> 00:07:08,931
Ugh.

82
00:07:09,890 --> 00:07:11,225
The things you do for love.

83
00:07:49,096 --> 00:07:51,014
I'm sorry for how I reacted.

84
00:07:55,143 --> 00:07:56,937
Good thing you
realized you were wrong.

85
00:07:59,356 --> 00:08:00,232
My fault?

86
00:08:01,775 --> 00:08:02,484
Yeah.

87
00:08:04,111 --> 00:08:05,070
Was that right?

88
00:08:05,404 --> 00:08:07,406
You got mad just
because I went out to eat?

89
00:08:07,406 --> 00:08:10,701
I was angry because you
left without informing me.

90
00:08:17,082 --> 00:08:17,958
Okay.

91
00:08:19,710 --> 00:08:20,711
Then I'm sorry too.

92
00:08:23,171 --> 00:08:26,091
Hey, but you know, I was
actually calling you earlier.

93
00:08:26,091 --> 00:08:27,509
You weren't answering.

94
00:08:27,509 --> 00:08:30,137
I was trying to call you,
but I couldn't get a hold of you.

95
00:08:31,888 --> 00:08:33,890
My battery was dead.

96
00:08:34,099 --> 00:08:36,435
How could you call me
if my battery was dead?

97
00:08:41,565 --> 00:08:42,232
Fine.

98
00:08:43,567 --> 00:08:44,276
I'm sorry.

99
00:08:44,276 --> 00:08:45,569
It was my fault.

100
00:08:48,947 --> 00:08:50,014
Okay.

101
00:08:50,407 --> 00:08:52,034
Apology accepted.

102
00:08:57,039 --> 00:08:59,583
Who were you with anyway?

103
00:09:06,423 --> 00:09:07,215
Hey!

104
00:09:07,215 --> 00:09:08,216
Zeke!

105
00:09:08,216 --> 00:09:09,051
Why?

106
00:09:09,926 --> 00:09:12,054
Do you see something I don't?

107
00:09:13,096 --> 00:09:14,056
Whoa?!

108
00:09:14,973 --> 00:09:15,682
Zeke!

109
00:09:16,099 --> 00:09:18,143
Your third eye is open.

110
00:09:18,143 --> 00:09:19,061
Stupid girl.

111
00:09:19,895 --> 00:09:22,522
I'm talking about the
dumbasses you had dinner with.

112
00:09:22,773 --> 00:09:23,648
Oh!

113
00:09:25,525 --> 00:09:26,401
Them.

114
00:09:26,735 --> 00:09:29,780
Uh, Phoenix and Cyd.

115
00:09:35,911 --> 00:09:37,245
Phoenix and Cyd, huh?

116
00:09:39,748 --> 00:09:40,791
Oh no.

117
00:09:41,124 --> 00:09:42,250
Oh no.

118
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:43,668
I'm so stupid.

119
00:09:43,668 --> 00:09:44,628
Oh no, don't—

120
00:09:44,628 --> 00:09:47,381
Don't tell them I told
you their names, okay?

121
00:09:47,672 --> 00:09:49,424
They said it was
supposed to be a secret.

122
00:09:49,424 --> 00:09:51,009
They have a surprise for you—

123
00:09:51,009 --> 00:09:51,843
Surprise?

124
00:09:52,135 --> 00:09:53,178
I'm so stupid.

125
00:09:53,929 --> 00:09:55,806
What else did you
guys talk about?

126
00:09:57,391 --> 00:09:57,933
Nothing much.

127
00:09:57,933 --> 00:09:59,976
They just taught me
how to play <i>pusoy dos</i>.

128
00:10:00,092 --> 00:10:01,000
And?

129
00:10:01,645 --> 00:10:02,813
And also, oh!

130
00:10:02,813 --> 00:10:04,314
We played truth or dare.

131
00:10:04,314 --> 00:10:06,817
Then whoever lost had
to answer questions.

132
00:10:10,028 --> 00:10:11,113
Questions like?

133
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:15,613
Like who killed Moo?

134
00:10:16,993 --> 00:10:19,454
Where does Roswell usually go?

135
00:10:20,872 --> 00:10:22,165
Have I met Yaji?

136
00:10:22,165 --> 00:10:23,708
Just stuff like that.

137
00:10:23,959 --> 00:10:24,960
They were really good.

138
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:26,336
They knew so much.

139
00:10:35,470 --> 00:10:36,555
Are you okay?

140
00:10:37,973 --> 00:10:40,267
Oh no, you're getting dizzy.

141
00:10:41,476 --> 00:10:44,938
That's what you get
for skipping meals.

142
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:46,773
You're so stubborn.

143
00:10:46,773 --> 00:10:48,150
Eat something first.

144
00:10:48,525 --> 00:10:50,652
Here, I got some takeout.

145
00:10:52,237 --> 00:10:53,039
Fries.

146
00:10:54,030 --> 00:10:54,698
Ah!

147
00:10:54,698 --> 00:10:56,408
Choo-choo!

148
00:10:56,658 --> 00:10:59,286
Choo-choo train!

149
00:11:00,287 --> 00:11:02,622
<i>Now arriving at Santolan Station.</i>

150
00:11:03,665 --> 00:11:06,001
<i>Now arriving at Santolan Station.</i>

151
00:11:07,919 --> 00:11:09,713
<i>The train's about to crash.</i>

152
00:11:11,590 --> 00:11:13,550
Open your mouth, Dong.

153
00:11:13,550 --> 00:11:15,677
There.

154
00:11:19,055 --> 00:11:20,682
You like being fed, huh?

155
00:11:21,516 --> 00:11:22,934
There, it's good, right?

156
00:11:42,412 --> 00:11:43,663
This looks familiar.

157
00:11:48,376 --> 00:11:49,169
Hey!

158
00:11:50,462 --> 00:11:51,922
Zeke, why do you have this?

159
00:11:54,424 --> 00:11:55,800
I gave this to Venice.

160
00:11:57,385 --> 00:11:58,386
Venice?

161
00:11:58,553 --> 00:11:59,446
Mmm.

162
00:11:59,471 --> 00:12:01,181
Shan Venice Birkins.

163
00:12:01,348 --> 00:12:02,682
Louie Birkins' twin.

164
00:12:04,893 --> 00:12:06,603
They're my friends from Stonehurst.

165
00:12:06,603 --> 00:12:07,979
Don't you know them?

166
00:12:10,148 --> 00:12:12,567
She asked me for this.

167
00:12:12,567 --> 00:12:14,569
She said she needed
it for something.

168
00:12:14,861 --> 00:12:16,363
But she said she'd
give it back right away.

169
00:12:16,363 --> 00:12:17,322
She promised.

170
00:12:25,997 --> 00:12:28,542
Can you promise me
not to trust anybody?

171
00:12:30,293 --> 00:12:31,253
Except me.

172
00:12:36,716 --> 00:12:37,559
Okay.

173
00:12:38,552 --> 00:12:39,497
Promise.

174
00:12:54,734 --> 00:12:57,112
Why are you sad? Want more fries?

175
00:12:57,279 --> 00:12:58,655
Here, have some more.

176
00:12:59,865 --> 00:13:01,157
Mm, eat some more.

177
00:13:04,077 --> 00:13:05,120
Good, right?

178
00:13:06,538 --> 00:13:07,872
There, chew it.

179
00:13:19,676 --> 00:13:20,614
Wife.

180
00:13:21,511 --> 00:13:25,056
I need the final updates on the plans
for the launching of your toy company.

181
00:13:25,849 --> 00:13:26,879
Can I get it?

182
00:13:29,686 --> 00:13:31,563
Final plan?

183
00:13:35,275 --> 00:13:36,042
Yes.

184
00:13:36,067 --> 00:13:37,193
For the launching event.

185
00:13:39,462 --> 00:13:41,005
Can I have a copy of your plans?

186
00:13:41,656 --> 00:13:42,465
It's been what?

187
00:13:42,490 --> 00:13:44,242
Two weeks since you
started working on it?

188
00:13:49,039 --> 00:13:50,540
I think she hasn't
done anything yet.

189
00:14:03,136 --> 00:14:03,928
Wife.

190
00:14:04,763 --> 00:14:05,889
I'm asking you.

191
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:12,062
Like I said, she clearly
hasn't done anything.

192
00:14:12,812 --> 00:14:14,731
I'll just finalize the guest list.

193
00:14:15,482 --> 00:14:19,152
Since Aemie clearly
hasn't even started it.

194
00:14:21,905 --> 00:14:23,948
Ms. Stonehurst, this is for you.

195
00:14:24,824 --> 00:14:26,618
Ah, finally.

196
00:14:26,938 --> 00:14:27,926
Thank you.

197
00:14:30,470 --> 00:14:31,388
Ezekiel,

198
00:14:33,583 --> 00:14:34,959
I brought you some lunch

199
00:14:35,627 --> 00:14:38,296
from a very fancy restaurant.

200
00:14:45,387 --> 00:14:48,682
It's pan-seared beef medallion

201
00:14:49,391 --> 00:14:51,643
with a side of potato puree.

202
00:14:53,645 --> 00:14:55,730
- I'm with Ms. Fiona.
- Me too, me too.

203
00:14:55,730 --> 00:14:56,638
No thanks.

204
00:14:57,228 --> 00:14:58,855
My wife brought our lunch.

205
00:15:00,068 --> 00:15:00,998
Right, wife?

206
00:15:01,820 --> 00:15:03,238
Ah, yes, hubby.

207
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:05,865
Yiee.

208
00:15:05,865 --> 00:15:07,200
Hubby, hubby.

209
00:15:18,128 --> 00:15:25,176
Allow me to present our
artisanal handheld beef creation

210
00:15:25,427 --> 00:15:29,556
layered in a toasted brioche vessel

211
00:15:29,848 --> 00:15:33,935
accompanied by golden
baton caught potatoes.

212
00:15:34,269 --> 00:15:38,022
delicately crisp to perfection.

213
00:15:39,315 --> 00:15:40,358
I'm with Aemie, sorry.

214
00:15:40,358 --> 00:15:41,818
Nope. Still Fiona.

215
00:15:44,345 --> 00:15:45,221
With collagen.

216
00:15:49,868 --> 00:15:51,119
That's a lot of fancy talk.

217
00:15:52,036 --> 00:15:53,079
It's just fast food.

218
00:15:55,039 --> 00:15:55,874
That's so...

219
00:15:56,332 --> 00:15:57,170
cheap.

220
00:15:57,792 --> 00:15:59,711
I mean, don't you think that like,

221
00:15:59,878 --> 00:16:00,378
I mean—

222
00:16:00,378 --> 00:16:01,129
I have a gun here.

223
00:16:02,255 --> 00:16:03,965
Do you want to meet
one of its bullets?

224
00:16:04,174 --> 00:16:05,884
Ohh.

225
00:16:08,887 --> 00:16:09,888
Whoa!

226
00:16:11,431 --> 00:16:12,432
Can they go on a date?

227
00:16:12,432 --> 00:16:13,808
A person and a bullet?

228
00:16:14,893 --> 00:16:16,352
Wife, my lunch.

229
00:16:16,895 --> 00:16:17,729
- Oh.
- I'm hungry.

230
00:16:17,729 --> 00:16:19,230
Okay, okay, okay.

231
00:16:20,023 --> 00:16:21,107
Say ah!

232
00:16:33,453 --> 00:16:34,287
Good?

233
00:16:34,287 --> 00:16:35,177
Good?

234
00:16:36,289 --> 00:16:37,332
One more?

235
00:16:42,086 --> 00:16:43,213
More, more!

236
00:16:57,602 --> 00:16:59,229
Airplane, airplane.

237
00:17:11,074 --> 00:17:12,283
Bro, do we still have a glass?

238
00:17:12,283 --> 00:17:12,992
You guys?

239
00:17:12,992 --> 00:17:13,993
There's a light over there.

240
00:17:15,203 --> 00:17:16,663
Go to the conference room.

241
00:17:16,955 --> 00:17:17,779
Now!

242
00:17:18,998 --> 00:17:20,625
We have to discuss something.

243
00:17:26,130 --> 00:17:26,731
Wife?

244
00:17:26,756 --> 00:17:27,590
Okay, okay.

245
00:17:27,590 --> 00:17:29,592
- More please.
- More? Okay.

246
00:17:29,717 --> 00:17:30,568
So you want more.

247
00:17:32,762 --> 00:17:33,638
Wow, good?

248
00:17:36,683 --> 00:17:38,434
French fries are your favorite?

249
00:17:48,653 --> 00:17:49,592
Lerwick.

250
00:17:50,321 --> 00:17:52,448
do you know the name of
the guys you were following?

251
00:17:53,783 --> 00:17:54,909
Those five assholes?

252
00:17:56,661 --> 00:17:57,631
Not yet, boss.

253
00:17:58,121 --> 00:17:59,581
But I'll find out as soon as possible.

254
00:17:59,581 --> 00:18:00,331
Never mind.

255
00:18:00,456 --> 00:18:01,499
How about you, Boulstridge?

256
00:18:02,417 --> 00:18:04,002
How's Aemie's mom been acting?

257
00:18:05,336 --> 00:18:06,154
Uhh.

258
00:18:06,838 --> 00:18:09,299
I haven't noticed anything
unusual about Ma'am Alyana, boss.

259
00:18:10,133 --> 00:18:10,881
Sure.

260
00:18:13,595 --> 00:18:14,498
Lee.

261
00:18:18,016 --> 00:18:19,017
Guardian Angel.

262
00:18:19,712 --> 00:18:22,279
Also known as Fauzia Arcadia.

263
00:18:22,729 --> 00:18:23,897
She's an assassin.

264
00:18:24,564 --> 00:18:27,692
And also, she's in the
same mafia group as Kevin Alferez.

265
00:18:28,610 --> 00:18:29,193
Wait.

266
00:18:30,236 --> 00:18:32,697
Those five assholes I've been
following are part of that too.

267
00:18:33,907 --> 00:18:35,408
But what I'm wondering is,

268
00:18:36,367 --> 00:18:37,785
why is Lionhart with them?

269
00:18:39,261 --> 00:18:40,856
Is he part of their group too?

270
00:18:43,053 --> 00:18:44,762
Lionhart, we're not sure of.

271
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:47,392
But Arcadia and Alferez

272
00:18:47,417 --> 00:18:50,336
are with the dumbasses, Cyd
Garnett, and Phoenix Strife.

273
00:18:51,455 --> 00:18:52,699
Who are those guys, boss?

274
00:18:53,157 --> 00:18:55,159
Those are the assholes
you've been following.

275
00:18:55,762 --> 00:18:56,696
Moron.

276
00:18:56,721 --> 00:18:58,431
Why don't we take those
guys down, Mr. Roswell?

277
00:18:59,414 --> 00:19:01,020
Do you want to die, Lamperouge?

278
00:19:02,915 --> 00:19:05,084
Don't fucking
meddle with my plans.

279
00:19:07,273 --> 00:19:08,358
Relax, Mr. Roswell.

280
00:19:09,192 --> 00:19:10,473
It's just a suggestion.

281
00:19:13,571 --> 00:19:14,387
Wait.

282
00:19:15,907 --> 00:19:17,659
So if those guys are
all in the same group,

283
00:19:19,077 --> 00:19:21,371
does that mean Fiona's
with them too, boss?

284
00:19:22,038 --> 00:19:22,997
You guess.

